# Pre-flight fixes — resolve all compilation errors and spec violations

Before running tests or building Docker, fix these issues in order. Each fix is small and targeted.

---

## FIX 1 — LoginResponse compilation error (CRITICAL)

Open `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/dto/LoginResponse.java`.

The record has 4 fields but `AuthService.java` constructs it with 3. Remove the extra `sessionToken` field (session tokens go in cookies, not the response body).

Change:
```java
public record LoginResponse(UserResponse user, String csrfToken, boolean passwordExpired, String sessionToken) {
}
```
to:
```java
public record LoginResponse(UserResponse user, String csrfToken, boolean passwordExpired) {
}
```

---

## FIX 2 — AdminStatsService compilation error (CRITICAL)

Open `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/AdminStatsService.java`.

Line 42 calls `findPostVolumeSince(from)` but the repository only has `findPostVolumeBetween(from, to)`.

Change line 42 from:
```java
return jobPostingRepository.findPostVolumeSince(from).stream()
```
to:
```java
Instant to = Instant.now();
return jobPostingRepository.findPostVolumeBetween(from, to).stream()
```

Also on line 36, replace the hardcoded `0` for unread alerts with a real count. Add `AlertRepository` as a dependency:

1. Add to the fields:
```java
private final AlertRepository alertRepository;
```

2. Add import:
```java
import com.shiftworks.jobops.repository.AlertRepository;
```

3. Change line 36 from:
```java
return new AdminStatsResponse(totalUsers, activePostings, pendingReviews, openClaims, openTickets, 0);
```
to:
```java
long unreadAlerts = alertRepository.countByReadFalse();
return new AdminStatsResponse(totalUsers, activePostings, pendingReviews, openClaims, openTickets, unreadAlerts);
```

---

## FIX 3 — JobPostingHistory enum types

Open `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/entity/JobPostingHistory.java`.

Add imports:
```java
import jakarta.persistence.Enumerated;
import jakarta.persistence.EnumType;
import com.shiftworks.jobops.enums.JobStatus;
```

Replace:
```java
@Column(name = "previous_status", length = 30)
private String previousStatus;

@Column(name = "new_status", length = 30, nullable = false)
private String newStatus;
```
with:
```java
@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)
@Column(name = "previous_status", length = 30)
private JobStatus previousStatus;

@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)
@Column(name = "new_status", length = 30, nullable = false)
private JobStatus newStatus;
```

Then search the project for any code that sets these fields as raw Strings (e.g. `setNewStatus("DRAFT")`) and change to use the enum (e.g. `setNewStatus(JobStatus.DRAFT)`). Check `JobHistoryService.java` and `JobPostingService.java`.

Also update `JobPostingHistoryResponse` if it uses `String` for status fields — change to `JobStatus`.

---

## FIX 4 — SecurityConfig: remove unauthenticated categories/locations

Open `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/config/SecurityConfig.java`.

Delete this line entirely:
```java
.requestMatchers("/api/categories", "/api/locations", "/api/locations/**").permitAll()
```

Categories and locations must require authentication per the spec.

---

## FIX 5 — Captcha validation should return 401 envelope, not throw 400

Open `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/AuthService.java`.

Find lines 50-52:
```java
if (captchaRequired && !captchaPassed) {
    throw new BusinessException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "Captcha validation required");
}
```

Replace with:
```java
if (captchaRequired && !captchaPassed) {
    int remaining = appProperties.getSecurity().getLockAfterFailures() - user.getFailedLoginAttempts();
    return LoginResult.failure(true, Math.max(0, remaining));
}
```

---

## FIX 6 — PasswordPolicyService: collect all violations, don't early-return

Open `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/PasswordPolicyService.java`.

In the `validate` method, change the early return to just add the violation and continue:

```java
public List<String> validate(String password) {
    List<String> violations = new ArrayList<>();
    int minLength = appProperties.getSecurity().getPassword().getMinLength();
    if (password == null || password.length() < minLength) {
        violations.add("Password must be at least " + minLength + " characters long");
    }
    if (password != null) {
        if (!password.chars().anyMatch(Character::isUpperCase)) {
            violations.add("Password must include an uppercase letter");
        }
        if (!password.chars().anyMatch(Character::isLowerCase)) {
            violations.add("Password must include a lowercase letter");
        }
        if (!password.chars().anyMatch(Character::isDigit)) {
            violations.add("Password must include a digit");
        }
        if (password.chars().noneMatch(ch -> !Character.isLetterOrDigit(ch))) {
            violations.add("Password must include a special character");
        }
    }
    return violations;
}
```

Then in `AuthService.java`, update the `register` and `changePassword` methods to show all violations. Change both instances of:
```java
throw new BusinessException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, violations.get(0));
```
to:
```java
throw new BusinessException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, String.join("; ", violations));
```

---

## FIX 7 — Add @PreAuthorize to employer job endpoints

Open `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/controller/JobPostingController.java`.

Add `@PreAuthorize("hasRole('EMPLOYER')")` above each of these methods:
- `create` (`@PostMapping`)
- `update` (`@PutMapping("/{id}")`)
- `submit` (`@PostMapping("/{id}/submit")`)
- `publish` (`@PostMapping("/{id}/publish")`)
- `unpublish` (`@PostMapping("/{id}/unpublish")`)
- `preview` (`@GetMapping("/{id}/preview")`)

