# Backup restore — complete the backend restore method and frontend handler

## File 1: Backend restore

Open `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/BackupService.java`.

Find the `restore(Long backupId)` method — it currently throws `UnsupportedOperationException` after the status check. Delete the `throw` line and the TODO comments, then add this implementation:

```java
try {
    Path filePath = Path.of(record.getFilePath());
    String[] dbInfo = parseDatabaseInfo();
    String host = dbInfo[0];
    String port = dbInfo[1];
    String dbName = dbInfo[2];

    SecretKeySpec keySpec = getKeySpec();

    ProcessBuilder pb = new ProcessBuilder(
        "mysql", "-h", host, "-P", port, "-u", dbUsername,
        "--password=" + dbPassword, dbName
    );
    pb.redirectErrorStream(true);
    Process process = pb.start();

    try (FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(filePath.toFile())) {
        byte[] iv = new byte[IV_BYTES];
        if (fis.read(iv) != IV_BYTES) throw new IllegalStateException("Invalid backup file");

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, keySpec, new GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_BITS, iv));

        try (javax.crypto.CipherInputStream cis = new javax.crypto.CipherInputStream(fis, cipher);
             GZIPInputStream gzip = new GZIPInputStream(cis);
             OutputStream mysqlIn = process.getOutputStream()) {
            gzip.transferTo(mysqlIn);
        }
    }

    int exitCode = process.waitFor();
    if (exitCode != 0) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("mysql restore exited with code " + exitCode);
    }
    log.info("Restore completed from backup {}", record.getFilename());
} catch (Exception e) {
    log.error("Restore failed for backup {}", backupId, e);
    throw new IllegalStateException("Restore failed: " + e.getMessage(), e);
}
```

The helper methods `parseDatabaseInfo()`, `getKeySpec()`, and the constants `IV_BYTES`, `GCM_TAG_BITS` already exist in the same file. The imports for `FileInputStream`, `GZIPInputStream`, `OutputStream`, `Cipher`, etc. are already at the top.

## File 2: Frontend restore handler

Open `frontend/src/views/AdminBackupsView.vue`.

Find the empty `handleRestore(row)` function. Replace with:

```javascript
async function handleRestore(row) {
  try {
    await ElMessageBox.confirm(
      `Restore from backup "${row.filename}"? This will overwrite current data.`,
      'Confirm Restore',
      { type: 'warning', confirmButtonText: 'Continue', cancelButtonText: 'Cancel' }
    );
    const { value: password } = await ElMessageBox.prompt(
      'Enter your password to confirm restore.',
      'Step-Up Verification',
      { inputType: 'password', confirmButtonText: 'Restore Now', cancelButtonText: 'Cancel' }
    );
    loading.value = true;
    await restoreBackup(row.id, password);
    ElMessage.success('Restore completed');
    await loadBackups();
  } catch (e) {
    if (e !== 'cancel') ElMessage.error(e?.response?.data?.message || 'Restore failed');
  } finally {
    loading.value = false;
  }
}
```

`ElMessageBox`, `ElMessage`, `restoreBackup`, `loadBackups`, and `loading` are already imported/defined in the file.

## Verify
Read `BackupService.java` restore method to confirm it no longer throws UnsupportedOperationException. Read `AdminBackupsView.vue` handleRestore to confirm it has the dialog flow.

