# Fix SQL injection + appeal crash

---

## FIX A — SQL injection in DashboardService

**File:** `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/DashboardService.java`

Find the status filter code (around line 231-234):

```java
if (!statuses.isEmpty()) {
    String statusList = statuses.stream().map(s -> "'" + s + "'").reduce((a, b) -> a + "," + b).orElse("");
    sql.append("AND jp.status IN (" + statusList + ") ");
}
```

Replace with enum-validated version:

```java
if (!statuses.isEmpty()) {
    List<String> safeStatuses = statuses.stream()
        .filter(s -> {
            try { com.shiftworks.jobops.enums.JobStatus.valueOf(s.toUpperCase(java.util.Locale.ROOT)); return true; }
            catch (IllegalArgumentException e) { return false; }
        })
        .map(s -> s.toUpperCase(java.util.Locale.ROOT))
        .toList();
    if (!safeStatuses.isEmpty()) {
        String statusList = safeStatuses.stream().map(s -> "'" + s + "'").reduce((a, b) -> a + "," + b).orElse("");
        sql.append("AND jp.status IN (").append(statusList).append(") ");
    }
}
```

---

## FIX B — Appeal processing passes null actor

**File:** `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/AppealService.java`

In the `processAppeal` method (around line 116), after the role check, add:

```java
User reviewerUser = userRepository.findById(reviewer.id())
    .orElseThrow(() -> new BusinessException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "reviewer: Not found"));
```

If `userRepository` is not already injected, add to the class fields:
```java
private final UserRepository userRepository;
```
And add: `import com.shiftworks.jobops.repository.UserRepository;`

Then replace both `null` calls. Change:
```java
jobHistoryService.record(jobPosting, JobStatus.APPEAL_PENDING, JobStatus.PUBLISHED, null, request.reviewerRationale());
```
to:
```java
jobHistoryService.record(jobPosting, JobStatus.APPEAL_PENDING, JobStatus.PUBLISHED, reviewerUser, request.reviewerRationale());
```

And change:
```java
jobHistoryService.record(jobPosting, JobStatus.APPEAL_PENDING, JobStatus.TAKEN_DOWN, null, request.reviewerRationale());
```
to:
```java
jobHistoryService.record(jobPosting, JobStatus.APPEAL_PENDING, JobStatus.TAKEN_DOWN, reviewerUser, request.reviewerRationale());
```

