# Fix password hash leak + audit immutability

---

## FIX A — Password hash leaks into audit logs

**File:** `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/entity/User.java`

Add `@JsonIgnore` to the `passwordHash` field. Find:

```java
@Column(name = "password_hash", nullable = false, length = 255)
private String passwordHash;
```

Change to:

```java
@JsonIgnore
@Column(name = "password_hash", nullable = false, length = 255)
private String passwordHash;
```

Add the import at the top: `import com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonIgnore;`

---

## FIX B — Audit trails are not immutable

**File 1:** `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/entity/AuditLog.java`

Add `@Immutable` to prevent Hibernate from updating records:

```java
import org.hibernate.annotations.Immutable;

@Data
@Entity
@Immutable
@Table(name = "audit_logs")
public class AuditLog {
```

**File 2:** `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/repository/AuditLogRepository.java`

Add delete guards to block deletion:

```java
public interface AuditLogRepository extends JpaRepository<AuditLog, Long>, JpaSpecificationExecutor<AuditLog> {
    List<AuditLog> findByEntityTypeAndEntityIdOrderByCreatedAtDesc(String entityType, Long entityId);

    @Override
    default void delete(AuditLog entity) {
        throw new UnsupportedOperationException("Audit logs are immutable");
    }

    @Override
    default void deleteById(Long id) {
        throw new UnsupportedOperationException("Audit logs are immutable");
    }

    @Override
    default void deleteAll() {
        throw new UnsupportedOperationException("Audit logs are immutable");
    }
}
```

