# Fix password rotation enforcement + cookie security

---

## FIX A — Password rotation is advisory only (not enforced)

**File:** `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/security/SessionAuthFilter.java`

The server returns `passwordExpired: true` in the login response but never blocks API access for expired passwords.

Read the file first. Find where `SecurityContextHolder.getContext().setAuthentication(...)` is called. Right after that line, before `filterChain.doFilter(request, response)`, add:

```java
if (user.getPasswordChangedAt() != null) {
    long daysSinceChange = java.time.Duration.between(user.getPasswordChangedAt(), java.time.Instant.now()).toDays();
    if (daysSinceChange > 90) {
        String requestPath = ((jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest) request).getRequestURI();
        if (!requestPath.equals("/api/auth/change-password") && !requestPath.equals("/api/auth/me") && !requestPath.equals("/api/auth/logout")) {
            ((jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse) response).setStatus(403);
            ((jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse) response).setContentType("application/json");
            ((jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse) response).getWriter().write("{\"code\":403,\"message\":\"Password expired. Please change your password.\",\"passwordExpired\":true}");
            return;
        }
    }
}
```

---

## FIX B — Session cookies hardcode secure(false)

**File:** `backend/src/main/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/controller/AuthController.java`

Find the two places where cookies are built with `.secure(false)`.

Replace both `.secure(false)` with:
```java
.secure("true".equals(System.getenv("COOKIE_SECURE")))
```

This defaults to `false` for local Docker but can be set via environment variable in production.

