# Fix 3 failing unit tests

---

## TEST FIX 1 — AuthServiceTest.java

**File:** `backend/src/test/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/AuthServiceTest.java`

**Problem A:** `LoginRequest` is a 4-component record (`username`, `password`, `captchaId`, `captchaAnswer`) but tests construct it with only 2 args.

Find every `new LoginRequest(username, "secret")` or `new LoginRequest(user.getUsername(), "secret")` (lines 82, 93, 107, 117) and change to 4 args with `null` for captcha fields:

```java
new LoginRequest(user.getUsername(), "secret", null, null)
```

Do this on lines 82, 93, 107, and 117.

**Problem B:** `loginCaptchaRequiredAfter3Failures` (line 112-121) expects `assertThrows(BusinessException.class, ...)` but the service now returns `LoginResult.failure()` instead of throwing.

Replace the entire test method:

```java
@Test
void loginCaptchaRequiredAfter3Failures() {
    User user = buildUser();
    user.setFailedLoginAttempts(3);
    when(userRepository.findByUsername(user.getUsername())).thenReturn(Optional.of(user));
    LoginRequest request = new LoginRequest(user.getUsername(), "secret", null, null);
    var result = authService.login(request, httpRequest(), false);
    assertFalse(result.isSuccess());
    assertTrue(result.failure().captchaRequired());
}
```

---

## TEST FIX 2 — JobPostingServiceTest.java

**File:** `backend/src/test/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/JobPostingServiceTest.java`

**Problem A:** `buildProps()` only sets `validityDays` and `hourlyPay` ranges. `headcount` and `weeklyHours` ranges default to [0,0], so headcount=5 or weeklyHours=40 will always fail validation.

In `buildProps()` (line 80-93), add the missing ranges after `validation.setHourlyPay(hourly);`:

```java
AppProperties.Range flatPay = new AppProperties.Range();
flatPay.setMin(50);
flatPay.setMax(10000);
validation.setFlatPay(flatPay);
AppProperties.Range headcount = new AppProperties.Range();
headcount.setMin(1);
headcount.setMax(500);
validation.setHeadcount(headcount);
AppProperties.Range weeklyHours = new AppProperties.Range();
weeklyHours.setMin(1);
weeklyHours.setMax(80);
validation.setWeeklyHours(weeklyHours);
```

**Problem B:** `submitTransitionsToPendingReview` (line 259-265) — `buildJob()` doesn't set `title` or `description`, so `validateExistingJob()` throws before the status change.

In `buildJob()` (line 113-127), add after `job.setStatus(status);`:

```java
job.setTitle("Valid Job Title");
job.setDescription("This is a valid job description longer than twenty characters");
```

Also set `validityStart` and `validityEnd` since `submitForReview` calls `validateDates`:

```java
job.setValidityStart(java.time.LocalDate.now());
job.setValidityEnd(java.time.LocalDate.now().plusDays(30));
```

---

## TEST FIX 3 — AnomalyDetectionServiceTest.java

**File:** `backend/src/test/java/com/shiftworks/jobops/service/AnomalyDetectionServiceTest.java`

**Problem:** `takedownSpikeGeneratesAlert` uses constant data (`2L` per day), making `stddev = 0`. The service returns early when `stddev == 0`, so the alert is never created and `verify(alertRepository, atLeastOnce()).save(...)` fails.

Replace `buildDailyData` and fix the test data to have variance:

Replace the `buildDailyData` method (lines 33-39):

```java
private List<Object[]> buildDailyData(int days, long baseCount) {
    List<Object[]> rows = new ArrayList<>();
    for (int i = 1; i <= days; i++) {
        long count = baseCount + (i % 3 == 0 ? 1 : 0);
        rows.add(new Object[]{Date.valueOf("2025-01-" + String.format("%02d", Math.min(i, 28))), count});
    }
    return rows;
}
```

In `takedownSpikeGeneratesAlert` (line 43), change today's count to be a clear spike — much higher than the mean + 2*stddev:

```java
when(reviewActionRepository.countTodayTakedowns()).thenReturn(50L);
when(reviewActionRepository.dailyTakedownsLast30Days()).thenReturn(buildDailyData(30, 2L));
```

This gives a mean around 2.3, stddev around 0.47, so today's count of 50 is well above mean + 3*stddev.

